From dca564fdcd363cebb5bb371b1bfdbb631b278a14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SB Team <noreply@succulentsbox.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:53:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] submit-signal: retry-safe client_submission_id on the
 hardened endpoint

Optional UUID from integrations that retry (Social Submission). Second dedup key
beside submission_key: stored ids are acknowledged without inserting; a
concurrent same-id insert (unique violation on that constraint only) is
re-checked and the rest of the batch inserted; skipped rows are verified to
exist before acknowledging; missing column -> 503, never false success; rows
without an id never touch the column. Keeps token auth, validation,
submission_key ON CONFLICT and bounded clustering unchanged.

Separate migration 20261029_signals_client_submission_id.sql (nullable column,
UNIQUE, format check, browser-write guard trigger). Tests: 8 endpoint cases on
the fake (extended for extra unique keys, missing columns, interleaving hooks)
and PostgreSQL checks in tests/db (idempotent migration, arbiter semantics,
unrelated violation, concurrency, browser users denied). Docs updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
